Status

LOCKED, appended to 0608. This amendment supersedes Section 2 of
0608_SERIES_600_UMBRELLA_OS_MODEL.md in full. Everything else in 0608
stands unchanged. Append this file immediately after 0608 in the
0000_SERIES-000-Governance tree, or merge Section 2 below directly into
0608 and retire this file — either is acceptable, but the content below
is the authoritative replacement for 0608's Section 2 as of this date.

Reason for amendment

0608 Section 2 described the money pipeline as Prospect → Excavation →
Dig Review → Dossier Production → Invoice, with invoicing treated as a
single missing terminal stage. This was an oversimplification, corrected
against the actual commissions.html structure and confirmed directly by
John. The original framing — "nothing upstream matters until money can
be collected at the end" — was backwards: money is collected first, at
Phase 0, before any Exhibit is even selected.

2. The money pipeline (department 1, the revenue path) — CORRECTED

Registry conversation (free, qualifying) → Phase 0 Shallow Dig
($2,500) → Exhibit selection (A–G, or enterprise tiers) →
five engagement stages (Habitat → Raw Stone → Cut & Shaped →
Mounted → Museum Display) → Delivery → optional CAMERA add-on
at any point after signal restoration.

2.1 Phase 0 is its own client record

The moment the $2,500 clears, that is a real, tracked client record —
independent of whether an Exhibit is ever subsequently selected. Phase
0's purpose is qualification, not "step one of the big engagement": it
weeds out non-serious prospects by being paid, and stays cheap/fast by
being shallow. A client can legitimately terminate at Phase 0 and never
proceed further. Phase 0 therefore needs its own lightweight lifecycle
(paid → in progress → delivered) that is NOT a sub-stage of the
five-stage engagement model — the two are separate state machines that
happen to chain together for clients who continue past Phase 0.

2.2 Payment is multi-point, not a single terminal stage

There is no single "invoice" stage. Payment events occur at multiple,
independent points:


Phase 0 payment ($2,500, qualifying)
Exhibit commission payment (on selection, bespoke per Exhibit A–G or
enterprise tier)
Retainer billing (recurring — applies to retainer-model Exhibits,
e.g. C, E, G)
CAMERA add-on payment (optional, any point after signal restoration)


The system needs a payment sub-state independent of engagement
stage, capable of firing more than once per client record, not a
single invoice flag at the end of a linear pipeline.

2.3 Engagement duration and exit are per-client, negotiated — not systemic

Whether and when a client exits Delivery/Museum Display is negotiated
per client and is not predictable or standardized. The system must NOT:


assume or display an expected timeline for any stage
treat time-in-stage as a signal of anything (stuck, overdue, healthy)
encode a default "end state" for the pipeline


A client sitting in Museum Display for two years is not an anomaly and
must not be flagged as one.

2.4 Implication for the pipeline-stage field (open item 4)

The 3-dimension field (exhibit_type, engagement_stage, retainer_status) still holds as the base design, but must additionally
support Phase 0 clients with exhibit_type = NULL — not yet
selected, or never proceeding further. Phase 0 is a distinct pre-Exhibit
state, not "stage 0" of the five-stage engagement model.

